  "id": "COMPOUND:23663 - PROTEIN:6020",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Phellandral, (R)- may interact with PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1 through multiple distinct pathways. The first pathway involves Phellandral, (R)- acting as a target of 5-O-Demethylpaxanthonin, which in turn targets CDC2L1. The second pathway links Phellandral, (R)- to UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B15, which is targeted by Marlignan J, also targeting CDC2L1. The third pathway shows Phellandral, (R)- targeting Electron transfer flavoprotein-ubiquinone oxidoreductase, which is targeted by Vertilecanin B methy ester, again leading to CDC2L1. These findings collectively indicate that Phellandral, (R)- may exert its biological effects through different molecular mechanisms, all ultimately leading to the modulation of CDC2L1. The evidence supports a potential role for Phellandral, (R)- in influencing the activity of CDC2L1, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
